WEBVTT

00:05.600 --> 00:08.610
Oh! Welcome, Mr. Denzel.

00:10.310 --> 00:11.240
Hmph.

00:12.150 --> 00:13.660
C'mon, sit over here!

00:13.660 --> 00:14.660
No way!

00:14.660 --> 00:15.920
I'm supposed to be meeting someone.

00:15.920 --> 00:18.080
What, a date? Good luck, buddy!

00:18.640 --> 00:19.620
Can I get coffee?

00:19.850 --> 00:22.040
If you get tongue-tied, call me on over!

00:22.040 --> 00:25.100
I've got just the thing to get the conversation going!

00:25.100 --> 00:26.130
A-ah...

00:30.020 --> 00:31.170
W-welcome!

00:32.480 --> 00:34.460
Could I have a cup of coffee?

00:34.460 --> 00:35.880
Sure! Right away!!

00:37.270 --> 00:38.250
Have a seat.

00:38.250 --> 00:39.430
Y-yessir!

00:43.350 --> 00:44.960
Well then, Denzel...

00:44.960 --> 00:47.890
I haven't much time so let's get straight to the point.

00:47.890 --> 00:51.330
I should warn you, we've changed the way we do things.

00:51.330 --> 00:55.150
We no longer accept just any volunteer.

00:55.450 --> 00:59.920
If you want to join the reconstruction effort, then it's better to contact the sector's supervisor.

00:59.920 --> 01:02.160
The WRO is a military unit now.

00:59.920 --> 01:02.160
WRO stands for World Regenesis Organization

01:02.710 --> 01:05.410
I understand. I don't care if it's dangerous.

01:05.410 --> 01:08.040
You've got the spirit. All right then...

01:08.050 --> 01:11.240
Let's hear what you've got... starting with your personal experience.

01:11.240 --> 01:12.850
My... experience...?

01:12.850 --> 01:15.760
I... uh... I'm only 10 years old...

01:16.010 --> 01:17.570
I know.

01:17.570 --> 01:20.260
But surely you've done something these 10 years?

01:21.130 --> 01:21.830
...eh?

01:24.290 --> 01:25.180
Mm...

01:37.700 --> 01:42.550
...in other news, we have the latest update about the attack on Mako Reactor No. 1...

01:42.550 --> 01:43.980
Where's mom!?

01:43.980 --> 01:45.980
Eh? She's out shopping.

01:46.840 --> 01:47.980
...I see

01:47.980 --> 01:49.420
I'm going to search for her.

01:49.560 --> 01:53.290
...with around 230 reported casualties...

01:49.700 --> 01:50.730
Huh?

01:52.210 --> 01:54.900
Shinra

01:54.900 --> 01:59.110
Hey, let go of me! What do you think you're doing?

01:59.110 --> 02:04.860
Sector 7 is going to be destroyed! So please, escape to Sector 5!

02:04.860 --> 02:06.620
I've got another place for us to stay.

02:07.120 --> 02:08.730
Destroyed!?

02:08.730 --> 02:13.980
The people behind the bombing of Mako Reactor No. 1 will go after No. 7 next!

02:15.210 --> 02:19.070
Is that true?! Then, we can't just run...

02:19.070 --> 02:21.740
We have to warn our friends and neighbors, too!

02:21.980 --> 02:23.910
There's no time, Chloe!

02:23.910 --> 02:27.060
Besides, this information is supposed to be top secret!

02:27.980 --> 02:32.250
I broke the rules to tell you... even though I'm the department head...

02:34.130 --> 02:34.750
Eh...?

02:35.720 --> 02:36.820
Denzel...

02:37.880 --> 02:39.760
Go on ahead with your father.

02:39.760 --> 02:42.240
I won't be long behind, okay?

02:42.240 --> 02:43.420
It'll be all right.

02:43.420 --> 02:44.300
Hey!!

02:48.490 --> 02:49.270
Ah--!

02:53.740 --> 02:56.150
Denzel, we've got to head to Sector 5.

02:56.150 --> 02:58.860
No! We gotta get mom!

02:58.860 --> 03:00.870
Mom will be fine.

03:01.250 --> 03:03.000
You can't blame her for caring.

03:04.280 --> 03:06.540
Chief! You're still here!?

03:07.220 --> 03:09.660
The Turks are on the move!

03:09.660 --> 03:12.900
They've probably set the bomb by now!

03:12.900 --> 03:16.160
I know since one of my buddies prepped their vehicle.

03:16.160 --> 03:18.340
Watch what you're saying out loud!

03:18.340 --> 03:20.470
Ah!! I'm sorry!!

03:21.910 --> 03:25.650
Arkham, could you take the kid to Sector 5 for me?

03:26.680 --> 03:29.240
Number 38 in the residential area.

03:29.240 --> 03:29.800
Uhm...

03:29.800 --> 03:30.620
No!!

03:30.620 --> 03:33.600
You will go with Arkham!

03:34.990 --> 03:37.610
Dad's going to bring mom home, okay?

03:37.950 --> 03:39.420
Dad!!

03:42.390 --> 03:44.600
I bought a brand new large-screen TV.

03:45.480 --> 03:48.450
You can watch whatever you like while you wait for us...

03:50.800 --> 03:56.550
...in response to this incident, Mr. Heidegger, head of Shinra Company's Public Safety Department...

03:56.930 --> 04:00.420
...asserted to reporters that AVALANCHE is behind this act of terrorism...

03:58.970 --> 04:00.670
I'm hungry.

04:01.020 --> 04:03.610
All righty, I'll get us something to eat!

04:11.710 --> 04:13.390
It's started...

04:15.510 --> 04:17.040
You wait here.

04:17.660 --> 04:20.380
Hey, wait! I'll go too!!

04:20.380 --> 04:22.610
This is an emergency report!

04:22.610 --> 04:26.220
A huge explosion has just occurred in Sector 7.

04:26.220 --> 04:27.120
...I repeat...

04:27.530 --> 04:31.300
A huge explosion has just occurred in Sector 7!

04:41.330 --> 04:44.100
Hey! It's dangerous out here! What are you doing?

04:44.820 --> 04:46.350
Where's your home, kid?

04:49.210 --> 04:50.120
Oh...

04:50.560 --> 04:51.830
I'm sorry...

04:52.730 --> 04:53.770
What about your parents?

04:58.920 --> 05:02.620
It was AVALANCHE that did this. Don't ever forget that.

05:02.620 --> 05:04.780
You can get your revenge when you grow up.

05:05.480 --> 05:08.300
Come on, we can't let you stay here.

05:13.480 --> 05:16.280
Was Shinra really behind those attacks?

05:16.280 --> 05:17.290
Yes...

05:18.260 --> 05:22.300
If you want someone to blame, go ahead and hate me.

05:37.100 --> 05:38.650
Shinra

05:47.660 --> 05:49.940
Hey! What're you doing!?

05:54.720 --> 05:56.410
Did you throw this?

05:59.830 --> 06:01.410
Why...?

06:03.640 --> 06:05.060
Are you crying?

06:07.440 --> 06:09.090
Where's your home, boy?

06:15.940 --> 06:18.140
Well, don't stand out here, come in.

06:19.630 --> 06:24.890
...Goodness gracious, I'll have my son fix this soon as he comes on home.

06:24.890 --> 06:27.050
This'll do for now.

06:27.590 --> 06:29.770
I'm sorry, Ms. Ruvie.

06:29.770 --> 06:34.370
If it weren't for all this ruckus, I'd been giving your parents a piece of my mind right about now!

06:34.370 --> 06:36.660
Mom... and dad are...

06:37.260 --> 06:41.220
There's no way they'd run and leave you on behind now, is there?

06:44.290 --> 06:46.170
They were... in Sector 7...

06:52.150 --> 06:55.310
Stay as long as you like, okay?

07:00.420 --> 07:03.310
Man... it's hot out here.

07:04.910 --> 07:06.870
What an adorable pattern.

07:06.870 --> 07:08.320
Looks like something a girl might carry.

07:11.010 --> 07:12.910
It does, doesn't it...

07:14.460 --> 07:15.910
Denzel!

07:16.490 --> 07:19.950
Here, try this on! I made it for you...

07:19.950 --> 07:22.410
Sorry about the design, it's all I had on hand...

07:22.410 --> 07:24.330
Thank you, Ms. Ruvie!

07:24.330 --> 07:26.810
Figured I'd use up some of that spare fabric I had lying around...

07:26.810 --> 07:28.590
Oh, and this too.

07:32.080 --> 07:36.680
Also... erm, this is really hard to put into words...

07:46.990 --> 07:51.320
I don't know much about it either, but seems that thing's called "Meteor"...

07:52.020 --> 07:57.130
They're saying if that thing hits our planet, we're all done for.

07:57.920 --> 08:02.790
For crying out loud, how do they expect us to prepare for the end of the world, hm?

08:04.190 --> 08:08.550
Denzel, I plan on spending the rest of my time right here.

08:09.080 --> 08:13.250
After all, if this planet's gonna be destroyed, it'll be the same no matter where I go.

08:13.250 --> 08:14.940
What would <i>you like to do?</i>

08:14.940 --> 08:19.560
If you wanna go someplace else, you're welcome to take as much food as you like.

08:19.960 --> 08:26.190
You may still be a little boy, but I think you deserve to choose where you'd like to spend what's left of your time.

08:30.160 --> 08:31.600
Is it okay...

08:31.600 --> 08:33.780
...if I stay right here?

09:00.590 --> 09:02.350
Ms. Ruvie... I'm scared!!

09:13.300 --> 09:15.110
Denzel!! Get back in that room!!

09:18.960 --> 09:19.990
Denzel!!

09:24.550 --> 09:27.290
Denzel, you stay in here, you hear?

09:27.660 --> 09:28.670
Ms. Ruvie--!!

09:55.780 --> 09:59.010
I don't know how long I was unconscious...

09:59.010 --> 10:01.950
When I came to, the entire room was a mess.

10:02.640 --> 10:04.750
Ms. Ruvie was on the floor.

10:04.750 --> 10:10.560
When I called her name, she opened her eyes a little and whispered "I'm glad you're okay"...

10:10.560 --> 10:13.460
She then said "Would you hold my hand?"

10:13.460 --> 10:16.880
I put out my hand and Ms. Ruvie took it, but...

10:16.880 --> 10:19.410
...she had a very weak grip.

10:19.410 --> 10:24.470
She said, "My son's hands are too big now, I can't hold them anymore".

10:24.950 --> 10:28.480
I think she was really happy to have a young child like me around.

10:29.270 --> 10:33.480
After that, she asked me, "How're things looking outside?"

10:34.310 --> 10:38.030
I was worried about her, but I went outside anyway.

10:38.030 --> 10:38.990
It was morning.

10:40.030 --> 10:44.490
The street was just as messy as the inside of the house was.

10:44.680 --> 10:48.430
Hey, Ms. Ruvie? ...Ms. Ruvie?

11:04.510 --> 11:06.320
AAAAAAAAH

11:17.480 --> 11:19.530
Daddy... save me...!

11:20.300 --> 11:22.530
Mommy... save me...!

11:22.530 --> 11:26.030
Mr. Arkham, save me...!!

11:33.000 --> 11:35.380
Hey! Quit sobbin'!

11:37.900 --> 11:42.930
What're you doin' here? Didn't you hear the TV's warning to evacuate to the slums?

11:43.820 --> 11:46.030
I... wasn't watching TV...

11:46.030 --> 11:47.310
Cripes!

11:47.310 --> 11:52.050
"I didn't know"... "I thought I'd be fine"... I'm sick of hearin' these stupid excuses!

11:52.950 --> 11:54.690
So? ...what about your family?

11:55.990 --> 11:58.690
Ms. Ruvie... is inside...

11:59.180 --> 12:00.430
Hm?

12:00.430 --> 12:02.700
His name was Gaskin.

12:02.700 --> 12:06.050
He dug a grave for Ms. Ruvie out back.

12:06.050 --> 12:08.870
Everyone in his truck helped too.

12:08.870 --> 12:13.210
She was buried with her sewing tools and her son's books.

12:13.910 --> 12:18.510
Everybody was surprised how thick the soil in the backyard was.

12:18.510 --> 12:21.210
They said that usually when you dig, you hit plate right away.

12:21.720 --> 12:25.300
I wonder if she was planning to grow vegetables in that garden?

12:25.300 --> 12:29.220
Many elderly people from the countryside are known to do something like that.

12:30.910 --> 12:32.220
No, it had to be flowers.

12:32.650 --> 12:35.680
The inside of her house was full of floral patterns,

12:35.680 --> 12:37.480
and she even had a lot of fake flowers.

12:38.150 --> 12:42.280
But she was probably looking for the real thing.

12:42.280 --> 12:47.270
Because her son was a Shinra employee, she was living in Midgar...

12:47.270 --> 12:52.070
...but I think all she really wanted was real soil that could support real flowers and...

12:52.070 --> 12:53.790
Ah... I'm sorry.

12:54.770 --> 12:56.510
I went off-topic.

12:57.590 --> 12:58.790
It's okay.

13:02.180 --> 13:05.800
The trains ain't running no more... and it don't look like they will ever again.

13:06.800 --> 13:11.250
But lucky for us, the rails are still intact.

13:11.250 --> 13:12.920
If we follow them, we can get down to the surface!

13:12.920 --> 13:15.270
You think Midgar is in danger?

13:15.270 --> 13:17.250
Beats me.

13:17.250 --> 13:20.190
But it's a surer bet that the surface is safer than up here, right?

13:20.590 --> 13:23.010
Watch your step!

13:23.010 --> 13:25.220
No one's got a moment to spare.

13:25.220 --> 13:27.450
So concentrate on fending for yourselves!

13:34.940 --> 13:35.660
Ah...!

13:36.450 --> 13:38.010
Mama...!

13:38.010 --> 13:40.460
Mama! Mama!

13:40.460 --> 13:41.890
It hurts, mama!

13:41.890 --> 13:43.670
H-Hey!!

13:43.930 --> 13:45.660
That kid's done for!

13:45.660 --> 13:48.330
Don't touch him! You'll catch it too!

13:51.860 --> 13:53.370
Where does it hurt?

13:53.370 --> 13:54.680
...behind...

13:55.030 --> 13:56.600
Your back, right?

13:56.600 --> 13:57.850
Uh-huh.

13:57.850 --> 14:03.110
Yes, no one knew a thing about the Geostigma Syndrome back then.

14:03.500 --> 14:07.270
The bodies of people who came into contract with Lifestream started to decay and eventually die.

14:07.270 --> 14:09.700
Many believed it was spread by physical contact...

14:10.120 --> 14:14.010
When in actuality, it was Jenova's cells mixed into the Lifestream that...

14:14.010 --> 14:18.210
...well, even if they had known the cause, it wouldn't have prevented the outcome.

14:18.570 --> 14:22.460
You're right. Especially... for the children...

14:23.430 --> 14:24.130
Yes...

14:30.640 --> 14:33.760
When I was traveling along the railroad tracks, I started thinking.

14:33.760 --> 14:36.100
"Boy, I wish I was a grown-up".

14:37.030 --> 14:41.460
I thought that if I was an adult, I'd have a lot more answers.

14:42.240 --> 14:42.760
Hey!

14:42.760 --> 14:43.190
Huh?

14:43.580 --> 14:45.120
Here's food. Eat up.

14:45.650 --> 14:46.740
But, t-that's...

14:46.740 --> 14:48.230
Scraps collected from the deceased.

14:48.230 --> 14:51.200
Ain't do them good anymore, right?

14:52.240 --> 14:54.550
You worried about catching that illness?

14:54.550 --> 14:57.060
Relax, the way it spreads is just a rumor.

14:57.060 --> 14:59.670
Well, it might be true, but...

14:59.670 --> 15:01.610
...nobody knows for sure right now.

15:02.100 --> 15:05.640
Besides, if you don't eat anything, you'll die anyway.

15:05.640 --> 15:09.260
If your gonna die, might as well die on a full stomach, y'know?

15:12.790 --> 15:14.230
Mmm... good.

15:14.230 --> 15:15.580
Still edible.

15:16.330 --> 15:18.520
It'd just rot if we left it lyin' on the ground.

15:18.520 --> 15:20.770
And that'd be a waste-- So eat!

15:24.200 --> 15:24.940
Thanks...

15:24.940 --> 15:25.770
Hm?

15:26.460 --> 15:27.220
Aha...

15:30.790 --> 15:32.740
I'd like some steel pipes...

15:32.740 --> 15:34.780
If possible, every last one here!

15:35.150 --> 15:36.470
Sure! Leave it to us!

15:36.470 --> 15:40.580
There isn't anything out there the Sector 7 Scavengers can't find!

15:40.580 --> 15:43.250
Yeah, that's why I came to you guys.

15:43.250 --> 15:45.790
You're famous around these parts.

15:46.410 --> 15:48.820
Edge's construction effort is coming along nicely, but...

15:48.820 --> 15:51.510
...we're all out of materials at the moment.

15:51.510 --> 15:54.000
Oh, right. Here, here... it ain't much, but...

15:55.090 --> 15:56.750
We'll take the job!

15:56.750 --> 15:59.460
I'm gonna go report in to Gaskin, 'kay?

15:59.460 --> 16:01.580
Let's go, Denzel. Time to work!

16:01.580 --> 16:02.310
Okay.

16:23.250 --> 16:26.500
Once we get enough cash, let's build our own home too!

16:30.150 --> 16:31.630
Mr. Gaskin...

16:31.630 --> 16:33.760
...died a month later.

16:34.440 --> 16:37.510
Everyone got together and buried him in a special place.

16:38.690 --> 16:41.900
All the good people... die first, don't they?

16:44.400 --> 16:46.500
As Edge's construction continued,

16:46.500 --> 16:49.240
and people learned how to smile again,

16:49.240 --> 16:53.400
the Scavenger's members also started to go their separate ways

16:53.400 --> 16:56.850
...including some children who died to the Geostigma.

17:00.920 --> 17:04.580
What can two people scavenge?
Screws and light bulbs?

17:04.580 --> 17:07.000
And we're not making much of a profit, either.

17:08.990 --> 17:12.980
Sigh... I guess it's time to move to Edge.

17:12.980 --> 17:15.180
They say you can get food for free!

17:15.470 --> 17:16.440
So that's it.

17:17.110 --> 17:18.560
Yup, that's it.

17:18.560 --> 17:20.550
I don't wanna die of starvation.

17:22.660 --> 17:24.740
How about we catch some rats to eat?

17:24.740 --> 17:25.940
Rats!?

17:26.470 --> 17:27.020
Yeah.

17:27.430 --> 17:33.070
Dad always said, because people are poor in the slums, they eat rats to survive.

17:33.820 --> 17:35.530
Filthy, grey rats...

17:36.030 --> 17:39.460
These are the slums... and we're poor, so...

17:40.490 --> 17:41.530
You're serious?

17:41.910 --> 17:44.600
Yeah. I'll eat a rat!

17:45.270 --> 17:47.540
I'm going to act like a real kid from the slums!

17:47.900 --> 17:50.330
We need a spear.

17:50.330 --> 17:52.910
Oh, really? Do it yourself!

17:52.910 --> 17:53.550
Rix...?

17:54.340 --> 17:56.880
I was born in the slums, for your information.

17:58.340 --> 18:00.390
I-I didn't know...

18:00.390 --> 18:02.600
Huh? What's the difference if you knew?

18:02.600 --> 18:04.390
You wouldn't have been my friend?

18:04.780 --> 18:06.140
That's not true!

18:06.140 --> 18:08.220
Keh! You say that now...

18:08.220 --> 18:11.650
You're just a spoiled brat who lived a comfy life up on the plate!

18:11.650 --> 18:12.860
Rix!

18:12.860 --> 18:14.350
Just remember this...

18:14.350 --> 18:17.320
Because of all the trash you dumped down on us,

18:17.320 --> 18:19.400
They got all sorts of crazy germs!

18:20.150 --> 18:23.370
There ain't a single idiot in the slums who'd dare to eat one!

18:27.300 --> 18:29.320
I didn't go after him

18:29.890 --> 18:32.280
because I didn't think he'd forgive me.

18:32.750 --> 18:33.920
Why's that?

18:34.280 --> 18:36.600
He was right. I was a kid from above.

18:36.600 --> 18:41.760
I was okay with the nearby slums and the area where Sector 7's ruins fell,

18:41.760 --> 18:45.160
but I never even considered visiting another part of the slums.

18:45.160 --> 18:51.060
I think the reason I didn't go to Edge was because I imagined it was like a slum.

18:51.060 --> 18:53.440
A dirty place full of poor people...

18:54.130 --> 18:55.230
How's Rix?

18:55.230 --> 18:56.550
He's fine.

18:56.550 --> 18:58.820
Still won't talk to me, though.

18:58.820 --> 19:02.450
That's great! You still have plenty of chances to make peace with him.

19:03.320 --> 19:06.680
I was serious about catching a rat to eat.

19:06.680 --> 19:09.480
I was out of a job and money.

19:09.480 --> 19:11.960
I was in a place even worse than the slums.

19:12.670 --> 19:16.340
If I kept on living like a kid from above, I'd never grow up.

19:16.630 --> 19:21.720
So I thought those diseased rats would be able to save me.

19:21.890 --> 19:23.090
W-w-w-what!?

19:23.340 --> 19:27.740
I believed it back then, but I realize I was wrong.

19:27.740 --> 19:29.490
And that's why I'm here today.

19:29.490 --> 19:31.100
W-well, I guess you could say that...

19:31.100 --> 19:33.600
...you mean because it was there you had the best encounter of your life?

19:34.300 --> 19:36.860
Yeah, even though it was in the worst of circumstances...

19:48.180 --> 19:49.120
Ah...

20:00.400 --> 20:03.800
I'm sorry, the number you're trying to reach in Sector 7 has been disconnected. Please try another number.

20:03.800 --> 20:04.660
Sigh...

20:14.840 --> 20:15.780
Cloud?

20:15.780 --> 20:18.090
It's rare to get a call from you.

20:18.090 --> 20:19.320
Did something happen?

20:20.740 --> 20:21.280
Huh?

20:22.040 --> 20:23.060
Cloud?

20:23.300 --> 20:24.510
It's not.

20:24.510 --> 20:26.510
Ah! ...who is this?

20:26.510 --> 20:29.290
You're... using Cloud's cell, right?

20:29.290 --> 20:30.330
I don't know.

20:30.330 --> 20:31.490
Who are you?

20:31.490 --> 20:33.490
I don't know! ...I...

20:33.660 --> 20:36.330
I don't know ...what to do!!

20:36.330 --> 20:39.210
Are you... crying?

20:39.690 --> 20:41.670
What's happening?! Are you okay!?

20:41.670 --> 20:44.720
Cloud? Cloud! Are you there!?

21:11.050 --> 21:13.630
I don't remember what happened after that.

21:13.630 --> 21:16.250
When I woke up, I was in bed.

21:16.250 --> 21:19.130
Tifa and Marlene were looking after me.

21:19.130 --> 21:21.390
...and I think you know the rest from there.

21:21.390 --> 21:22.460
Yeah, kinda...

21:23.290 --> 21:26.300
I owe my life now to many people.

21:26.660 --> 21:29.040
Mom and dad... Ms. Ruvie...

21:29.040 --> 21:31.400
Mr. Arkham and Mr. Gaskin...

21:31.680 --> 21:34.330
My friends from the Scavengers...

21:34.330 --> 21:35.770
many people who lived...

21:35.770 --> 21:37.770
...and many people who died...

21:37.770 --> 21:40.810
Tifa... Cloud... Marlene...

21:40.810 --> 21:42.360
...and I decided...

21:42.660 --> 21:43.350
Hm.

21:44.550 --> 21:47.400
I want to be someone like them for other people!

21:47.400 --> 21:50.070
It's my turn to protect others!

21:50.070 --> 21:52.470
...so, please let me join!!

21:52.470 --> 21:54.200
No way, no how!

21:54.200 --> 21:55.700
You shut up!

21:55.700 --> 21:57.700
You're just a kid!!

21:57.700 --> 21:59.670
That doesn't matter!

21:59.670 --> 22:01.560
No, actually...

22:01.560 --> 22:05.090
It was officially decided that children can't enlist in the WRO.

22:05.630 --> 22:06.810
See? Told ya!

22:06.810 --> 22:08.220
No way...

22:08.220 --> 22:11.090
Then... you should've told me no from the beginning!!

22:11.090 --> 22:13.330
No... because I came to my decision

22:13.330 --> 22:15.430
while listening to your past.

22:16.220 --> 22:19.710
There are some things that only children can accomplish.

22:19.710 --> 22:22.110
That's what I'd like you to focus on.

22:22.110 --> 22:23.110
Like what?

22:24.190 --> 22:26.610
Like bringing out the strength in us adults.

22:27.030 --> 22:27.670
Huh?

22:30.730 --> 22:32.800
Oh, and...

22:34.510 --> 22:34.990
Huh?

22:37.680 --> 22:40.430
Thanks for taking good care of mom.

22:52.060 --> 22:54.100
Sigh... you know, kiddo.

22:55.100 --> 22:58.950
If you wanna fight, you can do that anytime.

22:59.510 --> 23:02.600
There's no need to join the WRO for that!

23:02.600 --> 23:04.530
Why're you so hellbent about it?

23:04.530 --> 23:06.230
Because Cloud...

23:06.230 --> 23:08.110
What about Cloud?

23:08.630 --> 23:11.660
He's really strong because he was in the army.

23:11.660 --> 23:13.500
I want to be strong like him.

23:14.230 --> 23:17.490
Listen kid, times are changing.

23:17.490 --> 23:19.440
Changing how?

23:19.760 --> 23:20.870
How to put it...

23:21.530 --> 23:23.850
Instead of a guy who swings a weapon around,

23:23.850 --> 23:27.620
a guy who can be always be there to support people in rough times.

23:27.970 --> 23:30.510
That's the kind of guy all the ladies want in our day and age!

23:30.910 --> 23:33.510
Well I'm not trying to be popular with the ladies!

23:35.880 --> 23:37.000
Heh... haha!

23:38.160 --> 23:40.860
Ha ha ha!

23:41.030 --> 23:43.820
Hahahahaha!
